\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Blends collapse gradually through the layers. At each fork we feed a blend of the chosen token and the runner-up and measure how sharply each layer resolves it (snap: 0 = carried linearly, 1 = clean switch). Snap is 0 at the input by construction and reaches 0.98 (number vs word), 0.84 (number vs number) and 0.77 (word vs word) at the output. Number vs word snaps hardest at every layer from 1 to 28; number vs number starts slowest and passes word vs word at layer 13. Bands: 95\% bootstrap CIs over problems. 670 unique forks from 40 GSM8K problems (items 10--49). Inputs are sweeps between two candidates at forks, not the lopsided blends real runs feed (\cref  {sec:q3}).\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:snap}{{3}{5}{Blends collapse gradually through the layers. At each fork we feed a blend of the chosen token and the runner-up and measure how sharply each layer resolves it (snap: 0 = carried linearly, 1 = clean switch). Snap is 0 at the input by construction and reaches 0.98 (number vs word), 0.84 (number vs number) and 0.77 (word vs word) at the output. Number vs word snaps hardest at every layer from 1 to 28; number vs number starts slowest and passes word vs word at layer 13. Bands: 95\% bootstrap CIs over problems. 670 unique forks from 40 GSM8K problems (items 10--49). Inputs are sweeps between two candidates at forks, not the lopsided blends real runs feed (\cref {sec:q3}).\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig:snap@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][5][]5}}
