\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Neither Gumbel Soft Thinking nor the random-residual control differs detectably from sampling in accuracy; vanilla Soft Thinking trails it. Accuracy with Wilson 95\% CIs. McNemar: exact two-sided test on the problems where exactly one of the pair is correct (arm only / sampling only). Exp\nobreakspace  {}16: sampling and Gumbel Soft Thinking at seeds 0 and 1, vanilla Soft Thinking at seed 0; McNemar uses the seed 0 runs, the only seed vanilla has. Vanilla hit Cold Stop on 14 of 30 runs, and all 5 runs without an answer ended there; against Gumbel (seed 0) it is 1 vs 5, $p = 0.22$. Exp\nobreakspace  {}23: seed 0; the three arms share their noise, and the random-residual control moves the residual to a random token. Problems in Exp\nobreakspace  {}23 are not used in any other experiment.\relax }}{10}{table.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:accuracy}{{1}{10}{Neither Gumbel Soft Thinking nor the random-residual control differs detectably from sampling in accuracy; vanilla Soft Thinking trails it. Accuracy with Wilson 95\% CIs. McNemar: exact two-sided test on the problems where exactly one of the pair is correct (arm only / sampling only). Exp~16: sampling and Gumbel Soft Thinking at seeds 0 and 1, vanilla Soft Thinking at seed 0; McNemar uses the seed 0 runs, the only seed vanilla has. Vanilla hit Cold Stop on 14 of 30 runs, and all 5 runs without an answer ended there; against Gumbel (seed 0) it is 1 vs 5, $p = 0.22$. Exp~23: seed 0; the three arms share their noise, and the random-residual control moves the residual to a random token. Problems in Exp~23 are not used in any other experiment.\relax }{table.caption.26}{}}
\newlabel{tab:accuracy@cref}{{[table][1][]1}{[1][9][]10}}
